Q1. MCQ — Stream Basics

Which statement about a Java Stream is correct?



A. A Stream stores elements permanently like a Collection
B. A Stream can modify the original Collection automatically
C. A Stream is used to process elements from a data source
D. A Stream can always be reused after a terminal operation



Correct Answer: C ✅



Reason: A Stream provides a pipeline for processing elements from a source such as a Collection, array, or I/O channel. It does not permanently store elements.

Q2. Output Based — filter()

List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(10, 15, 20, 25, 30);

list.stream()
    .filter(x -> x > 20)
    .forEach(x -> System.out.print(x));


What is the output?



A. 102030
B. 2530
C. 2030
D. 15202530



Correct Answer: B ✅



Reason: Only values greater than 20 pass the filter: 25 and 30.

