Q19. Mutable vs Immutable — collect()

List<Integer> original =
    new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3));

List<Integer> result =
    original.stream()
            .map(x -> x * 10)
            .collect(Collectors.toList());

result.add(40);

System.out.println(result);


What happens?



A. Compilation error
B. Runtime exception because Stream results are immutable
C. 40 is successfully added
D. Original list also automatically gets 40



Correct Answer: C ✅



Reason: Collectors.toList() does not promise an immutable List. The resulting List can support add(), and original is not automatically modified.

